            "controller_support": "full",
            "detailed_description": "<strong>IAH: INTERNET WAR</strong> is a tactical roguelite that combines turn-based planning with real-time squad combat. Stop ZENDAR CORP from placing the world under the control of a global AI. Play solo or in online co-op for 2 to 10 players.<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >EXPLORE THE INTERNET</h2><br>Navigate a labyrinth of connected rooms containing websites, enemies and valuable resources. Capture Control Panels to secure territory and unlock illegal contracts.<br><br>Every action advances one turn. Browse the network, buy equipment, build bots or move deeper into the labyrinth, and the internet responds.<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >FIGHT IN REAL TIME</h2><br>Command your bots on a 3D battlefield. Move them, select targets, set combat stances and use their skills. Cover, flanking and line of sight affect every fight. Tactical Mode gives you direct control when precision matters.<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >SURVIVE THE RESPONSE</h2><br>Completing contracts increases your wanted level. Police become stronger, rival hackers trace you and enemy crews attack your operation.<br><br>Each wave presents three Chaos cards, and you must choose one. Counter their effects with weapons, equipment, items and permanent upgrades.<br><br>Protect your Main Bot. If it dies, the run ends. Your score unlocks new hackers, bot improvements and crafting parts for future runs.<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >FEATURES</h2><br><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li>Single-player and online co-op for 2 to 10 players<br></li><li>A labyrinth of rooms and websites to explore<br></li><li>Turn-based planning and real-time tactical combat<br></li><li>Cover, flanking, line of sight and direct unit control<br></li><li>400+ Chaos cards, weapons and items<br></li><li>100+ bots and structures<br></li><li>Eight hackers with different bots, bonuses and drawbacks<br></li><li>Bot crafting and permanent progression</li></ul>",
            "about_the_game": "<strong>IAH: INTERNET WAR</strong> is a tactical roguelite that combines turn-based planning with real-time squad combat. Stop ZENDAR CORP from placing the world under the control of a global AI. Play solo or in online co-op for 2 to 10 players.<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >EXPLORE THE INTERNET</h2><br>Navigate a labyrinth of connected rooms containing websites, enemies and valuable resources. Capture Control Panels to secure territory and unlock illegal contracts.<br><br>Every action advances one turn. Browse the network, buy equipment, build bots or move deeper into the labyrinth, and the internet responds.<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >FIGHT IN REAL TIME</h2><br>Command your bots on a 3D battlefield. Move them, select targets, set combat stances and use their skills. Cover, flanking and line of sight affect every fight. Tactical Mode gives you direct control when precision matters.<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >SURVIVE THE RESPONSE</h2><br>Completing contracts increases your wanted level. Police become stronger, rival hackers trace you and enemy crews attack your operation.<br><br>Each wave presents three Chaos cards, and you must choose one. Counter their effects with weapons, equipment, items and permanent upgrades.<br><br>Protect your Main Bot. If it dies, the run ends. Your score unlocks new hackers, bot improvements and crafting parts for future runs.<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >FEATURES</h2><br><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li>Single-player and online co-op for 2 to 10 players<br></li><li>A labyrinth of rooms and websites to explore<br></li><li>Turn-based planning and real-time tactical combat<br></li><li>Cover, flanking, line of sight and direct unit control<br></li><li>400+ Chaos cards, weapons and items<br></li><li>100+ bots and structures<br></li><li>Eight hackers with different bots, bonuses and drawbacks<br></li><li>Bot crafting and permanent progression</li></ul>",
            "short_description": "IAH: INTERNET WAR is a tactical roguelite combining turn-based strategy and resource management with real-time squad combat. Explore a labyrinth of website-filled rooms, customize combat bots, and fight ZENDAR CORP solo or in online co-op for 2 to 10 players.",
